<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaboyo Olimi I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaboyo Olimi I was the founder of the Kingdom of Toro in western Uganda. A son of Omukama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyamutukura-kyebambe-iii">Nyamutukura Kyebambe III</a> of Bunyoro, he rebelled around 1830 and set up an independent kingdom in the fertile lands around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwenzori-mountains">Rwenzori Mountains</a>. Toro's later kings descended from him.</p></div>
